---
<Layout headExtra={headExtra}><main id="main-content" class="seo-page classic-blog-reading"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><span class="breadcrumb-separator" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></span><a href="/blog">Blog</a></li><li><span class="breadcrumb-separator" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></span><a href="/blog/adult">Adult Mental Health</a></li><li><span class="breadcrumb-separator" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></span><span aria-current="page">Psychologist vs psychiatrist for depression</span></li></ol></nav><article><p class="seo-kicker">Adult mental health</p><h1>Psychologist vs psychiatrist for depression</h1><div class="blog-answer"><strong>In short:</strong> A psychiatrist can assess medical factors and discuss medication when appropriate, while a psychologist or counsellor may provide psychological assessment and therapy. The right starting point depends on the person’s symptoms, safety, preferences, and clinical needs.</div><h2>What each professional may offer</h2><p>Psychiatric assessment may consider mood, sleep, physical health, medicines, substances, family history, and safety. Psychological work may focus on thoughts, behaviour, relationships, coping, and patterns that affect daily life.</p><h2>When support may be coordinated</h2><p>Some people benefit from therapy, some from a medical review, and some from both. Coordination should be based on assessment rather than a promise of a particular outcome or treatment.</p><h2>Questions to ask</h2><ul><li>What will the first appointment cover?</li><li>How will safety and follow-up be handled?</li><li>What options are available if the first plan does not fit?</li></ul><p>If you are unsure where to begin, read the <a href="/psychiatrist-vs-psychologist">comparison guide</a> or explore <a href="/depression-treatment-ncr">depression assessment information</a>.</p></article></main></Layout>
